  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "[Followup from Sourceforge Tracker]",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Followup Submitter: cwilper",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Logged In: YES ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "user_id=189298",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Originator: YES",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Blair has submitted the necessary changes to PolicyEnforcementPoint.java and PolicyFinderModule.java",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "On Feb. 5, 2007, Blair wrote:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The major additions are in the PolicyFinderModule where the cache",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "operations code lives.  The reason for changing the",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "PolicyEnforcementPoint too is that PolicyFinderModule initialisation",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "had to be reworked to load the repository wide policies when the init",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "method is called (this is done by sunxacml when the PDP is created).",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Because the init method is declared in the sun code it couldn't throw",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "an exception if loading of repo wide policies failed, thus I had to",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "add a check that is called after the PDP is constructed.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "There are several customisable parameters that might be worth exposing",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "in fedora.fcfg:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "the max cache sizes (that is the number of AbstractPolicies of each",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "type": "hardBreak"
             },
             {
              "text": "type, Policy or PolicySet, that can be cached at any time), currently",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "type": "hardBreak"
             },
             {
              "text": "100 of each;",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "the referenced policies directory, currently this is set to be",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "type": "hardBreak"
             },
             {
              "text": "\"referenced-policies\" at the same directory tree level as the",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "type": "hardBreak"
             },
             {
              "text": "\"repository-policies\" directory (currently if the directory does not",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "type": "hardBreak"
             },
             {
              "text": "exist it will NOT be created);",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         },
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "text": "the cache decay rate, this is the time in milliseconds it takes to",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "type": "hardBreak"
             },
             {
              "text": "reduce an inactive cache entry's weight by 1 (currently 1 minute).",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "type": "hardBreak"
             },
             {
              "text": "The weight is used to select a row to replace on a cache miss when the",
              "type": "text"
             },
             {
              "type": "hardBreak"
             },
             {
              "text": "cache is already full.",
              "type": "text"
             }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         }
        ],
        "type": "bulletList"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "During testing I came across a rather strange behaviour which I think",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "may be a bug in the javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder.  When a",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "reference is included in a repo wide policy or another referenced",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "policy like so:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "<PolicyIdReference>",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "policy.xml",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "</PolicyIdReference>",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "it works fine.  However when the same lines are included in a FOXML",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "object's POLICY datastream they cause an invalid URI exception on any",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "access attempt (making the object unreadable), this seems to be due to",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "the new line after the opening element.  Removing the formatting makes",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "the problem go away:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "<PolicyIdReference>policy.xml</PolicyIdReference>",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Certainly the new line is invalid in a URI however it doesn't seem to",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "be passed along when read from a file, the only difference being which",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "DocumentBuilder.parse method is called.  Just something to be aware of",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "if/when idreference examples make it into the system documentation.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
